\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we synthesize the elicitation criterion}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{We synthesize the criterion in \ref{ftip-0005} from two recurring
observations. First, reinforcement learning can move probability toward
successful traces that a base model already emits; this possibility is tested
empirically in
\citet{secs. 2.3 and 3.3--3.4}{liu2025understanding}. Second, a finite experiment
cannot establish that an unrestricted generative model assigns exactly zero
probability to a behaviour. The positive threshold
#{\varepsilon} therefore belongs to the declared experiment rather than to an
ontological claim about what the model ``contains.''}

\p{Later questions ask how an elicitation witness changes with the sampling
budget, decoding rule, and reward. A useful theorem would bound the attainable
increase in #{p_1(B)} from the starting probability #{p_0(B)} and the
information supplied by post-training.}
